WEBVTT

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.610
What's the weakness of his weapon?

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.450
2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.490
He stopped.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.880
Well, of course.
Obviously he can use both arms.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.000
This won't be easy.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.960
He shoots 9 times from each arm.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.260
I can't get close.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.680
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.720
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.890
And the gears turn

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.070
When the horn blows, the flames dance

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.990
The story waits for no-one

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.870
Off they go, the gears are churning

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.120
A red past chases after you

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.460
The jester's smile

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.340
What's behind the mask?

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.170
You can't erase the scars

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.050
No matter how they burn

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.890
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.930
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.730
Alone in the depths of the night

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.820
Let out a cry that can cut through fate

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.360
That's the cue to begin

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.860
The curtain is rising, it's time to dance

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.040
Everybody sheds tears at the end

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.120
So hold them in now and keep going

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:48.750
Until the day the curtain falls

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:54.090
The gears will keep turning

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.560
#23 The demon's return

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.150
Your rotation axis
is losing balance already.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:19.490
Your molybdenum steel alloy
is like paper compared to my cross carbon.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.490
I'm not done yet!

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.120
See? Undone in a second.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.620
Damn it.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.540
Too slow.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:38.800
It was much too easy to beat you.
I couldn't even answer your question.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.680
But since we're here, I'll tell you.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.480
Why I've sided with Lord Faceless.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.060
It's simple.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:56.070
Earth is the most magnificent planet
in this universe.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.740
And I couldn't bear the irrationality
of how humans live on it.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.490
This is a beautiful planet.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.540
But on it lives a certain species.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:12.750
One that contributes nothing
and devours everything.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.000
Humans.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.260
I realize now.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.760
The earth can remain beautiful
only if humans disappear from it.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:30.060
You see?
Humans must first be immobilized.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.980
Once that happens,
they will finally be of some use.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:40.240
As food for the automata
who will clean the earth up.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.950
But the automata say that
shirogane blood is nasty.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.040
So you're good for nothing at all.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.330
My, my.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.580
You fool.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.260
What's wrong, puppeteer?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.350
Les Mains Vertes Foncées shoots
blasts of pressurized air.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.760
No ammo to run out of.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.220
Thanks for telling me.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.980
But I'm a professional assassin.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.530
This is my job, I can't run away from it.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.280
My only chance is when he changes arms.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.280
But his moves aren't impossibly fast.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.330
The automata's golden rule? What's that?

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:37.210
Ashihana, you said you couldn't win
against the automata.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.840
But the golden rule is your answer.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.010
The key to winning.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.010
I don't get it.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.470
Originally,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:52.390
automata were made as clowns
to bring fear and suffering upon humans.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.940
That means humans are their audience.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:59.940
The audience must be able to see them.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.620
You mean, they can't move at a speed
we can't see.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.490
Exactly, not as long as
humans are the audience.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:15.290
But if people hold weapons or ride tanks,
they cease to be an audience.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.790
I see.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.260
That's why shiroganes fight
with marionettes.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.340
Because marionettes aren't weapons.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:29.510
Right. That means
as long as you fight using marionettes,

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.890
the automata can only move
at a human-like speed.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.940
That's why you can win
against the automata.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.900
I sure don't feel like I can.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.160
But I'll give it a try!

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.290
Your marionette moves likes it's dancing.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.830
Not bad.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.040
6, 7, 8, 9.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.380
Now!

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.630
Not so fast, puppeteer.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.010
This is where I wanted you!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.470
Up in mid-air!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:10.300
You think so?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.970
He moved?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.530
You did well human, but not well enough.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.030
Damn it!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.080
Pathetic. Here, have it back.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.120
There you go.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:54.640
According to Tom, Harry is pretty big.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.930
How do you plan to carry it?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.350
Fou's given orders.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.150
Ashihana and George will transport it.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.910
Blood! Fresh blood for everyone!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.790
How could you!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.790
I can't hear you, you bug.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.050
Let's stomp them all.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.640
-Stop!
-As if I would...

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.060
It's just a human!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.230
A human? Wrong.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.070
He's no human...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.320
No human could be as strong as that.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.710
What the heck are you?

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.210
I'm a demon.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.020
Are you all okay?
I'm glad you're still alive.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.650
I'm Narumi.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.820
Yes, I know.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.990
Excuse us,
but we don't have any time, Miss Helen.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.910
Do you know where Harry is?

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.580
We can't let the automata
get their hands on it.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.920
Down that hall.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.550
Narumi, I'll stay here.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:51.130
I'll keep the automata away.
You get Harry.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:58.810
They're still not giving up?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.230
They should just hand Harry over,
don't you think?

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.360
Right, Blom Blom Low?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.190
Take it easy, Drill September.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.860
Gotta hand it to them.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:17.320
They're only humans,
but they've used their brains.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.620
They're pretty smart.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.880
Modifying the machine to emit waves
that nullify the ZONAPHA bug.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:32.590
Since we live on fluids
made with the ZONAPHA bug,

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.510
we can't get close to it.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.640
A true master researcher of ZONAPHA.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.640
Doctor, the magnetic field
is growing smaller.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:41.640
I know.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.150
But Lord Faceless
is going to be mad at us.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.310
We need to hurry and take it home.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.360
That's why I'm sitting here waiting.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:57.490
The limit situation Jaspers wrote about
in this book is closing in on them.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:02.370
It's a situation
they can't do anything about.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:07.630
Nobody's coming to help.
It's the end for them.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.460
The battery is going to die.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.210
Don't give up.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.380
Remember when this institute
was on the verge of destruction?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.800
The man who fought by himself
to save the children.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.680
We must be like him.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.540
What is your name, puppeteer?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.250
It's Ashihana. Why do you ask?

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:53.420
You were quite skilled as a puppeteer.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:58.180
I thought I'd ask you your name
before I killed you.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.430
Well, thanks.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.970
Guess it's over for me.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:08.480
With this huge sword stuck in me...

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:13.020
Wait a second, that's it.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.320
But old man, I'm just a regular person.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.160
How could I ever beat the automata?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.910
Regular, you are not.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:28.160
You drank George's blood
at the battle in the Sahara.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.670
There is Aqua Vitae
flowing in shirogane blood.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:39.430
Even a few drops
can spread throughout the body.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.220
It doesn't make you a shirogane,
but it'll make you tougher.

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:45.930
What's more..

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:49.440
For automata, Aqua Vitae is...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.060
That's it.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:57.150
So long as my name's Eiryo Ashihana,
I've got to give this a shot.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.400
It's not my usual style, but...

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.090
You fool, you'll die anyway.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.010
Why go through all that pain?

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.010
Well...

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:29.640
I don't like being pinned
like a bug specimen.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.600
Goes against my style.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.150
Besides, I've already been paid.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:40.820
20 billion yen in advance.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:45.410
About three more steps, I think.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.790
What's that?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.750
Anyway, farewell Ashihana.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.590
Why do you laugh?

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.170
You're so square.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.470
Way too square.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:08.010
I'd rather be killed by someone
a bit more clever.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.020
What did you say?

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.730
By the way...

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.980
you've never been liked by a woman,
have you?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.990
What do you mean by that?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.280
Easy.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:28.370
To have a woman want to see you again.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:33.370
I'm an automaton.
Such matters mean nothing to me.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.210
I can tell.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:40.000
I bet you've never even made
a woman smile.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:47.510
Being able to make a woman smile
is the first step to making them like you.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.730
Come with me.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.730
Help me find a way for me to smile.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:03.240
For this, I have given you
a will of your own.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:12.120
What? Aren't you going to kill me?

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:18.420
There is a lady that I must make smile.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.960
But how do I do it?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:26.970
Human smiles can be explained by
the superiority theory, incongruity theory

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.930
and relief theory.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:32.060
No no, Mr. Pantalone.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.390
If you want to make a woman smile,

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.520
forget those theories.

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:43.900
Tell me! How can I make her smile?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.950
I'll tell you.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:52.120
But I'm almost at the end of my life.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:56.200
I can't speak up anymore...

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.880
Will you come closer?

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.380
Say it.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.890
A little closer.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:15.390
Just a bit more now.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:17.890
Good.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.860
Here goes.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.480
This is how you make women smile.

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.740
What's this?

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:31.910
Don't you get it?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.500
A hug is worth a million words.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:42.460
You gotta show it with your body
or women won't smile for you.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:51.840
Aqua Vitae is poisonous for automata.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.440
Sorry there.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.860
But it's all your fault.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.370
For telling me to move out of your way.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:23.330
Impossible... I can't move my body!

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.380
Oh, it's the blood!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.340
There's Aqua Vitae in that human's blood.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:38.430
But he hasn't seen the last of me yet!

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.770
Really? Still going at it?

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.860
I'm all out of ideas now.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.450
Too bad. Guess this is it for me.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.080
Die, Ashihana!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:02.210
I will never forgive you
if you hurt another human.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.470
What was that?

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.850
He missed on purpose?

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.360
Your pride and your body are in tatters.

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:34.240
Give up already. I'll take your pain away.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.370
Give up?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:44.080
I thought machine humans
never cracked jokes.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.250
Smoking?

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.800
You're a shirogane-O.
That's much too irrational.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.010
I got bored.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:57.680
Of living rationally and
of being bored of my own life.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.010
What are you saying?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.680
You remind me of myself in the past.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:08.110
I used to believe I was chosen by God.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.520
So what?

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:12.190
But you're not me entirely.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:18.070
I was asked to play the piano.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.080
I don't understand you.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:25.040
I was applauded as they asked me.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:28.880
To play the piano again.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:32.460
Have you gone mad? Well then.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.510
I'll kill you and
the rest of the humans inside.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.260
They asked me.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.010
Me, they asked me!

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:51.650
What? My Wunderkugel is being overpowered.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.280
Impossible.
You can't have that much power left.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.030
You've never been asked that.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.570
Why is he picking up speed?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.950
He's going to surpass my speed!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:07.460
But they asked me!
Those children asked me!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.460
Will you play the piano again?

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.140
You can't hear it.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.560
It doesn't exist
in the earth you wish for.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.150
The most beautiful music ever.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:10.850
I'm not so fond of these after all.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:17.400
You shouldn't smoke
if you don't really want to.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:24.370
Oh? What's wrong with me?

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:29.330
I'm suddenly feeling so sleepy.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:37.000
No, I don't want to yet...

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.590
I want to stay awake...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.810
Now, what next?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:58.610
What shall I play for them?

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:04.030
For those children...

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.920
I've never seen you look so regretful.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.630
Never in all this time.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.050
Dr. Banhart!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.310
Who are you?

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.390
Puppet...

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:35.060
We win.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:40.480
You'll never get Harry.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.570
Just two plain humans against us?
Don't make me laugh.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:51.830
You'll see if I'm a plain human or not.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:59.090
Hurry up or the others will drink up
all the blood!

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.760
The party is over.

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:10.010
And you weren't invited.

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:32.080
Avoiding the crowds, I walk in the dark

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:36.960
And wait with bated breath in the wings

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:41.710
My expression is calm
while I scream inside

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:46.550
On the verge of being torn apart

00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:51.470
I dance and beckon you to join me

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:56.350
As a shadow swings across the stage

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:59.350
I tell myself this is the last time

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:05.360
But I can't seem to cut myself free

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:09.780
Too scared to stop for a moment

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:15.290
My impatience hides
the cries of somebody left behind

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:23.750
Nobody notices the shadow
standing in the sudden rain

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:31.850
Somewhere far away,
a memory of you is saying goodbye

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:39.310
I stand here watching,
no longer able to reach you
